  "prompt": "Ciarán, the marketing director, must explain the paid media overspend to finance on Friday and needs Q3 2025 budget against actual for each paid channel and month. The budget plan sets a budget for each paid channel and month. A channel's actual spend in a month is what its campaigns spent on the UTC days of that month, and Q3 2025 runs from 2025-07-01 to 2025-09-30. Return one row for each paid channel and month of Q3 2025 in the budget plan, a budget of 0 euros included, keeping a channel and month with no spend, with eight columns in this order: month, the first day of the month; channel_id; channel_name; budget_eur, the planned budget in euros; actual_eur, the actual spend in euros, not rounded, and 0 when the channel spent nothing that month; variance_eur, actual_eur minus budget_eur, so an overspend is positive; variance_pct, 100 times variance_eur divided by budget_eur, rounded to 1 decimal, and missing when budget_eur is 0; and flag, 'over' when variance_pct is above 10, 'under' when it is below -10, and 'on_track' otherwise, a missing variance_pct included. Sort by month from early to late, then by variance_eur from high to low, then by channel_id from low to high.",
